    "sourceUrl": "https://revelatedesigns.com/product/magtank/",
    "sourceCheckedAt": "2026-09-02",
    "manufacturerDetails": "The Legacy Mag-Tank™ features a smartly contoured top flap secured by a magnetic buckle with mechanical engagement, ensuring no accidental openings, even when your bike is upside down. With one-handed operation, simply pull the cord loop outward for full top access; closing is a breeze with a simple flick of the flap. \nThe Legacy Mag Tank excels at fast on-the-go access to calories and electronics and now includes a TPU liner built from the same material as hydration bladders. The liner is easily detachable with velcro for post ride cleaning. No more sticky food messes after your long rides – just pure convenience and functionality.\nPlease note: While the cover to this bag is designed to shed rain and spray, due to the large panel opening it is not a fully sealed bag or waterproof bag. Additionally, while the closure is secure there is the possibility that small objects can come out of the bag from rough trails or lying the bike on its side. A key clip is integrated into the bag but we recommend keeping your gummy bears in a ziplock.\nCheck out the Bikepacking.com review ( plus their review for the TPU liner ) or the Path Less Pedaled video review !\nDimensions\n\nUS \nMetric \nHeight (H)\n5 in\nLength (L)\n8.5 in\nStem Width (W)\n2.5 in at stem; tapers to 1.5 in at rear\nHeight (H)\n127 mm\nLength (L)\n216 mm\nWidth (W)\n64 mm at stem; tapers to 38 mm at rear\nSpecifications\n\nUS \nMetric \nWeight (oz)\nVolume (in³)\nWithout TPU Liner\n4.5 oz\n55 in³\nWith TPU Liner\n5.5 oz\n55 in³\nWeight (g)\nVolume (L)\nWithout TPU Liner\n128 g\n.9 L\nWith TPU Liner\n157 g\n.9 L\nMaterials: Challenge EPX 200 C0 Recycled polyester laminate with EPX 400 C0; 200 denier recycled polyester lining; closed cell foam padded tube sections. HDPE sheets. Imported.\nReviews",
    "description": {
      "en": "The Legacy Mag-Tank™ features a smartly contoured top flap secured by a magnetic buckle with mechanical engagement, ensuring no accidental openings, even when your bike is upside down. With one-handed operation, simply pull the cord loop outward for full top access; closing is a breeze with a simple flick of the flap. \nThe Legacy Mag Tank excels at fast on-the-go access to calories and electronics and now includes a TPU liner built from the same material as hydration bladders. The liner is easily detachable with velcro for post ride cleaning. No more sticky food messes after your long rides – just pure convenience and functionality.\nPlease note: While the cover to this bag is designed to shed rain and spray, due to the large panel opening it is not a fully sealed bag or waterproof bag. Additionally, while the closure is secure there is the possibility that small objects can come out of the bag from rough trails or lying the bike on its side. A key clip is integrated into the bag but we recommend keeping your gummy bears in a ziplock.\nCheck out the Bikepacking.com review ( plus their review for the TPU liner ) or the Path Less Pedaled video review !\nDimensions",
      "ru": "Сумка на верхнюю трубу Revelate Designs объёмом 0.9 L. Характеристики нормализованы по официальной карточке товара."
    },
