    "sourceUrl": "https://revelatedesigns.com/product/nanopanniers/",
    "sourceCheckedAt": "2026-09-02",
    "manufacturerDetails": "When you need the cargo capacity that a rack provides, but want something that won’t get in your way when the going gets rowdy, Nano Panniers are the ticket.\nAt only 4″ wide the load stays tight to the bike on singletrack and will not get in your way on those nasty hike-a-bikes. An external compression system keeps the bag snug at various load levels.\nThe magic is in the details on our rack attachment system. Although simple in concept, the tight spacing between the aluminum loop and strap prevents slop at the pannier rails. A bomber Voile nano strap with metal hardware provides tension at the bottom and gives versatility in mounting.\nThink of these bags as frame bag supplements that stay on your bike; designed to carry dense and heavy stuff like food, water, and fuel with a low profile form. With a bikepacking mindset you still put your bulky, high water sensitive items like clothing, sleeping and shelter gear in a waterproof handle bar setup, seat pack, or on top of the rack deck.\nDimensions\n\nThese panniers are not compatible with “T” style racks. In talking with rack manufacturers most lack the load capacity and means for a lower attachment.\nIf your rack has external bolt mounts or other braze-ons that protrude where the panniers rest, you’ll need to pad them or cover with tape to prevent damage to the inner fabric of the panniers.\nThese panniers are designed to be mounted and held in tension. On racks such as Salsa’s Alternator series, they should be mounted in the higher position.\nUS \nMetric \nHeight (A)\n10 (max 16)\nLength (B)\n10.5 in\nC\n2 in\nD\n5.75 in\nE\n.5 in\nWidth\n4 in\nHeight (A)\n254 (max 406.4)\nLength (B)\n266.7 mm\nC\n55 mm\nD\n145 mm\nE\n10 mm\nWidth\n101.6 mm\nSpecifications\n\nUS \nMetric \nWeight (oz)\nVolume (in³)\nPair\n18 oz\nEach side 420-680 in³\nWeight (g)\nVolume (L)\nPair\n510 g\nEach side 11 L\nMaterials: Challenge Sailcloth 200 denier UHMWPE / Polyester woven with PET film lamination.\nMade in the USA with domestic and imported materials\nReviews",
    "description": {
      "en": "When you need the cargo capacity that a rack provides, but want something that won’t get in your way when the going gets rowdy, Nano Panniers are the ticket.\nAt only 4″ wide the load stays tight to the bike on singletrack and will not get in your way on those nasty hike-a-bikes. An external compression system keeps the bag snug at various load levels.\nThe magic is in the details on our rack attachment system. Although simple in concept, the tight spacing between the aluminum loop and strap prevents slop at the pannier rails. A bomber Voile nano strap with metal hardware provides tension at the bottom and gives versatility in mounting.\nThink of these bags as frame bag supplements that stay on your bike; designed to carry dense and heavy stuff like food, water, and fuel with a low profile form. With a bikepacking mindset you still put your bulky, high water sensitive items like clothing, sleeping and shelter gear in a waterproof handle bar setup, seat pack, or on top of the rack deck.\nDimensions",
      "ru": "Панир Revelate Designs объёмом 11 L. Характеристики нормализованы по официальной карточке товара."
    },
