    "manufacturerDetails": "To address the needs of long-distance ultra racing, the Pitchfork Aerobar System provides load carrying and storage for essentials that you want quickly at hand.\nThe Pitchfork is a 2-part holster system featuring gigantic stretch woven side pockets with a removable 6 Ultra 200 denier dry bag. The pockets easily swallow light clothing layers and can securely stow calories from a gas station resupply. To optimize the size of the pockets, the holster wraps over the bars rather than strapping underneath. This allows for bigger pockets and provides fast access to a flat platform top-mounted bungee system. Everything is designed for quick access and all cords are field replaceable for the long haul.\nTo accommodate different bar spacing, pairs of laser cut hypalon slots are built into the holster to change the strap mounting width.\nThe seam taped Ultra 200 UHMWPE dry bag has an asymmetrical tapered bottom for stem clearance and is sized to fit a light sleeping/shelter system or warm clothing and rain gear. A removable front strap can be used to tension the front of the dry bag if using it fully packed on rough terrain. The dry bag is secured to the holster with spring-loaded, non-dangling auto cam buckles.\nUpdate for Spring 2026 – Upgraded holster fabric, DP DX40 UHMWPE. White is faster and looks sick!\nCheck out Bikepacking.com’s review of the Pitchfork here. \n*Note: aerobars are not included* \nDimensions\n\nUS \nMetric \nHolster (A)\n7.25 in\nDrybag Length (B)\n12 in\nDrybag Width (C)\n6 in\nBar spacings (D)\nAdjustable between 3.5 - 5 in\nHolster (A)\n184 mm\nDrybag Length (B)\n305 mm\nDrybag Width (C)\n152 mm\nBar spacings (D)\nAdjustable between 89 - 127 mm\nSpecifications\n\nUS \nMetric \nWeight (oz)\nVolume (in³)\n6 oz\nDry Bag :366 in³; Pockets each side: 61 in³\nWeight (g)\nVolume (L)\n170 g\nDry Bag: 6L; Pockets each side: 1 L\nMaterials: Holster: Challenge EPX 200 laminate; Ultra Stretch - UHMWPE reinforced stretch woven pocket fabric; 1.0mm TPU - Hypalon. Drybag: Challenge Ultra 200 UHMWPE woven.\nMade in the USA\nReviews",
