    "manufacturerDetails": "It’s back and better than ever! The Pronghorn is a race focused, lightweight handlebar system for the minimalist bikepacker. Without sacrificing functionality, the Pronghorn is a stripped-down bar mounted carrying system.\nPersonally tested and refined by Revelate designer Dustin Eroh on the Colorado Trail Race, Kenai 250, and many more — the Pronghorn has garnered distinction from the racing community for its stable and simple functionality since its initial release in 2018. A key to the system’s performance is a strategically placed internal fiberglass stay that is integrated into both the mounting points and front dry bag attachment straps. This keeps your load from shifting while navigating technical singletrack.\nThe latest Pronghorn update can be found in the dry bag. The design is now double-ended, allowing for easier access to the contents of your bag! Made from Challenge Ultra 200 UHMWPE this waterproof bag comes in three sizes to fit every kind of adventure. Please note that in order to retain full waterproof functionality, you’ll need to roll the ends of the dry bag at least three times.\nWhen standing at the starting line of your next race, or sprinting to the hills on a fast and light bender, the Pronghorn is the most efficient solution for your gear carrying needs.\nDimensions\n\nThe rule of thumb is to keep a lighter load on your handlebars for better handling. The small / medium are best for ultra races in warm climates and multi-day single track trips. Bigger is not better; choose the smallest bag you can get away with. The small is for a dialed ultralight kit and racing. The medium is the most versatile size. The large is specifically designed for winter trips to fit a -20 down sleeping bag.\nDisk or V Brake only – NOT compatible with Cantilever or road style front brakes with a vertical exposed cable.\nNote for using the Pronghorn with drop bars: You may need to roll the bag more than 4 times on each side to reduce the length to fit your available space, thus reducing the overall volume from what is listed. You may want to size up to retain volume.\nDimensions of a closed bag with 4 rolls at closure:\nUS \nMetric \nLength\nWidth\nHeight\nSM\n16.25 in\n5.5 in\n4.5 in\nMD\n19 in\n7 in\n6.5 in\nLG\n24 in\n8.5 in\n7.5 in\nLength\nWidth\nHeight\nSM\n419 mm\n140 mm\n114 mm\nMD\n483 mm\n178 mm\n165 mm\nLG\n610 mm\n216 mm\n191 mm\nSpecifications\n\nUS \nMetric \nWeight (oz)\nVolume (in³)\nSM (w/o pocket clips)\n7.5 oz\n458 in³\nMD (w/o pocket clips)\n8.2 oz\n671 in³\nLG (w/o pocket clips)\n9.2 oz\n1404 in³\nSM (w/ pocket clips)\n8.4 oz\nMD (w/ pocket clips)\n9.1 oz\nLG (w/ pocket clips)\n10.1 oz\nHolster only\n4.9 oz\nWeight (g)\nVolume (L)\nSM (w/o pocket clips)\n213 g\n7.5 L\nMD (w/o pocket clips)\n232 g\n11 L\nLG (w/o pocket clips)\n252 g\n23 L\nSM (w/ pocket clips)\n238 g\nMD (w/ pocket clips)\n258 g\nLG (w/ pocket clips)\n286 g\nHolster only\n139 g\nMaterials: Holster: VX21Blue; Drybag: Challenge Ultra 200 UHMWPE.\nReviews",
