    "sourceUrl": "https://revelatedesigns.com/product/spinelock10/",
    "sourceCheckedAt": "2026-09-02",
    "manufacturerDetails": "We set out to create the most stable, low profile mounted, feature loaded, waterproof bikepacking saddlebag available. The Spinelock™ seat bag checks all the boxes.\nThe Spinelock integrates user tested and approved features like a one-way air purge valve, rear light slots, loop and bungee deck, and an external plastic bottom with a new patented attachment system. Stability was the driving element in the design process. If you want something you can pack and forget, the Spinelock is your seat bag.\nThere are two size options, neither of which sacrifice features for capacity. The smaller but largely versatile Spinelock 10L maximizes your carry with minimal tire clearance and provides a generous amount of waterproof storage with additional space on the external corded deck. . If you are going on a long expedition or carrying cold weather gear, we recommend checking out the Spinelock 16L .\nHow it works: \nThe Spinelock stability system consists of three components: the saddle clamp, seat bag mounted “Spine” baseplate, and pin.\nA low profile, high strength, forged aluminum clamp works in combination with precision IGUS bushings to form the pin interface. Twin forged upper arms, fastened by Torx-25 bolts, rotate into position above the saddle rails for easy mounting.\nResembling a spine ramp familiar to skateboarders, the “Spine” baseplate is made of an impact resistant UV-stabilized nylon and is integrated to the seat bag surface. The plate features two mounting positions to accommodate seatpost setback and saddle adjustments. To connect the bag, you simply line up your selected mounting position to the seat mounted clamp and slide the pin through the aligned holes. Attaching the side compression straps to the wings of the clamp fixes the pin in place, and you’re ready to ride!\nWinner of the 2020 Gear of the Year Awards! See what Bikepacking.com has to say: Spinelock review. \nDimensions\n\nImportant information on use and fit: \nTraditional saddle style rails are required.\nNot compatible with carbon fiber saddle rails.\nOnly compatible with traditional style saddle rails and is not compatible with most models of Brooks saddles(B17, B66, B67, Flyer, and similar) as well as other branded saddles with similar flared rail styles. If using a saddle with flared seat rails, we recommend considering the Terrapin Seat Bags. \nThis product is not designed for use with dropper seat posts.\nNOT compatible with suspension seat posts.\nThis bag is for carrying soft, pliable objects. Sufficiently pad any hard edge objects like cookware to prevent premature wear.\nIt is mandatory to check tire clearance prior to use, especially with full suspension bikes. Always check for tire clearance with your suspension at full travel.\nBag contact with a tire can cause a bad wreck and ruin your day. Tire damage to the bag is not covered by warranty.\nA Torx-25 wrench is needed for installation. You likely already have one on your multi-tool!\nUS \nMetric \nMinimum tire clearance (A)\n8 in\nMinimum exposed seat post (B)\n6.5 in\nMinimum tire clearance (A)\n200 mm\nMinimum exposed seat post (B)\n164 mm\nSpecifications\n\nUS \nMetric \nWeight (oz)\nVolume (in³)\n22.5 oz\n610 in³\nWeight (g)\nVolume (L)\n638 g\n10 L\nMaterials: 210 Denier Ripstop Nylon with dual coated TPU, urethane based Hypalon reinforcement fabric, UV-stabilized, impact resistant nylon resin, forged aluminum. Imported.\nReviews",
    "description": {
      "en": "We set out to create the most stable, low profile mounted, feature loaded, waterproof bikepacking saddlebag available. The Spinelock™ seat bag checks all the boxes.\nThe Spinelock integrates user tested and approved features like a one-way air purge valve, rear light slots, loop and bungee deck, and an external plastic bottom with a new patented attachment system. Stability was the driving element in the design process. If you want something you can pack and forget, the Spinelock is your seat bag.\nThere are two size options, neither of which sacrifice features for capacity. The smaller but largely versatile Spinelock 10L maximizes your carry with minimal tire clearance and provides a generous amount of waterproof storage with additional space on the external corded deck. . If you are going on a long expedition or carrying cold weather gear, we recommend checking out the Spinelock 16L .\nHow it works: \nThe Spinelock stability system consists of three components: the saddle clamp, seat bag mounted “Spine” baseplate, and pin.\nA low profile, high strength, forged aluminum clamp works in combination with precision IGUS bushings to form the pin interface. Twin forged upper arms, fastened b",
      "ru": "Подседельная сумка Revelate Designs объёмом 10 L. Характеристики нормализованы по официальной карточке товара."
    },
